                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ce95817c-903d-3579-bae2-f0ac0cf07867",
                        "entry_id": "6ae0f7d5-c57d-36c8-bbc2-b40ad0a0de2d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор. титул крупных мусульманских аристократов в Индии"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f27a435f-5e98-485b-b2fa-1bad3d1de7e9",
                                "sense_id": "ce95817c-903d-3579-bae2-f0ac0cf07867",
                                "text": "Сумасбродный и расточительный князь, влюбленный в княжну, давно на нее сорил деньгами, как индийский набоб."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "83189706-a3fc-306f-8a2b-8cc198156410",
                        "entry_id": "6ae0f7d5-c57d-36c8-bbc2-b40ad0a0de2d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "о быстро разбогатевшем человеке (первоначально о дельце, разбогатевшем в колониях)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0cb1bdbb-d3c4-4a11-9be2-9fd3bc1f39cd",
                                "sense_id": "83189706-a3fc-306f-8a2b-8cc198156410",
                                "text": "Два милліона доходу… Больше, говорятъ! Золотые пріиски, рыбныя ловли, хлѣбные экспорты… Словомъ, набобъ."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ac94bba3-e4c8-4a6d-ab7e-20aef0397c24",
                        "source_entry_id": "6ae0f7d5-c57d-36c8-bbc2-b40ad0a0de2d",
                        "target_lang_word": "nabob",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "nabob",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7f9b8324-3dc0-3fdf-b62b-0041511b1134",
                                        "entry_id": "98c5c1a5-6eb7-3707-a965-dfe646e04854",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An Indian ruler within the Mogul empire."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a640f388-6309-4def-b189-9dfa87d8bf1e",
                                                "sense_id": "7f9b8324-3dc0-3fdf-b62b-0041511b1134",
                                                "text": "They have drained the treasuries of Nabobs, who must fill them by oppressing the industry of their subjects."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4ee980c7-d95e-3678-9e1e-17d43f4e5631",
                                        "entry_id": "98c5c1a5-6eb7-3707-a965-dfe646e04854",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone of great wealth or importance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "181676d6-fb39-467d-a09b-da56b18130cd",
                                                "sense_id": "4ee980c7-d95e-3678-9e1e-17d43f4e5631",
                                                "text": "Mr. Glentworth had never quitted Europe, and his wealth was either good English landed property, or equally undeniable English consols; still he was a stranger, very rich, and suddenly come from abroad. Such a man was necessarily a nabob in Mr. Palmer's eyes. India had been the place for making large fortunes in his young days."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a16be87-1b7a-4c49-ab7a-7cec103c822a",
                                                "sense_id": "4ee980c7-d95e-3678-9e1e-17d43f4e5631",
                                                "text": "Private-equity nabobs bristle at being dubbed mere financiers. Piling debt onto companies’ balance-sheets is only a small part of what leveraged buy-outs are about, they insist. Improving the workings of the businesses they take over is just as core to their calling, if not more so. Much of their pleading is public-relations bluster."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3c8381d7-7899-3bae-b23a-f949a32c8abd",
                                        "entry_id": "98c5c1a5-6eb7-3707-a965-dfe646e04854",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person with a grandiose style or manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b3f1b607-6692-49c9-a17d-9437920942bd",
                        "source_entry_id": "6ae0f7d5-c57d-36c8-bbc2-b40ad0a0de2d",
                        "target_lang_word": "nabab",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "nabab",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "69aac0b3-3674-340a-a7a9-f9ee700f2d02",
                                        "entry_id": "dd9b4888-ac70-34a8-aabc-7aba5cf6a16f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Virrey o gobernador provincial en el imperio Mogol."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "853dcda7-e528-4ece-bc30-245b5b09d5a3",
                                                "sense_id": "69aac0b3-3674-340a-a7a9-f9ee700f2d02",
                                                "text": "A ejemplo de los subás, sacudieron también el yugo de la obediencia de los nababes que dependian de ellos."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74e5efc0-4f17-4cfc-9f0d-1a8a7395e7f1",
                                                "sense_id": "69aac0b3-3674-340a-a7a9-f9ee700f2d02",
                                                "text": "...los sucesores de Tipoo-Saib en Misora y los nababs de Bengala y de Hidrabab."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7a659ac2-8a2e-3cec-977c-ba2502e4f571",
                                        "entry_id": "dd9b4888-ac70-34a8-aabc-7aba5cf6a16f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "En general, noble o príncipe musulmán bajo el dominio colonial británico en la India."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "98670068-9472-3317-a380-6df70a960419",
                                        "entry_id": "dd9b4888-ac70-34a8-aabc-7aba5cf6a16f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Hombre de fortuna fabulosa."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"3\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4d47a485-2fbd-4b40-98ca-e7bb5d0a1591",
                        "source_entry_id": "6ae0f7d5-c57d-36c8-bbc2-b40ad0a0de2d",
                        "target_lang_word": "nababo",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e8226d18-3e2a-4995-9317-3ced7e000e25",
                        "source_entry_id": "6ae0f7d5-c57d-36c8-bbc2-b40ad0a0de2d",
                        "target_lang_word": "nabab",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "nabab",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ffc3987e-9fb0-3140-a4e6-55d4ee7acba0",
                                        "entry_id": "9ec632a7-f2db-3a7a-ae0c-c4a7a14079b3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Prince dans l’Inde moghole."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e82e18b-e04f-47ad-be31-75a9e1dcd888",
                                                "sense_id": "ffc3987e-9fb0-3140-a4e6-55d4ee7acba0",
                                                "text": "Le nabab de Visapour traitait alors avec le pescha, chef de la République maratte, de la levée de plusieurs escadrons qu'il voulait prendre à sa solde."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9ffabaf-ec58-48a5-8f74-663c2dcfdf19",
                                                "sense_id": "ffc3987e-9fb0-3140-a4e6-55d4ee7acba0",
                                                "text": "C’est quelque nabab qui arrive de l’Inde."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eb9078b9-effe-359e-989a-39843223aff3",
                                        "entry_id": "9ec632a7-f2db-3a7a-ae0c-c4a7a14079b3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personne riche."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33386ec8-75b7-445f-a98e-c040ef625d3d",
                                                "sense_id": "eb9078b9-effe-359e-989a-39843223aff3",
                                                "text": "On venait pour apprendre les dernières informations de l’Action parallèle, pour voir le dernier homme que Diotime, comme on disait, s’était fait venir, un nabab allemand, un riche Juif, un original qui écrivait des poèmes, dictait les cours du charbon et fraternisait avec l’empereur d’Allemagne."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a858d22-7ec2-4b2e-847a-2ac0463f955a",
                                                "sense_id": "eb9078b9-effe-359e-989a-39843223aff3",
                                                "text": "Hydra, par les temps qui concourent, rappelle une cité interdite. Jamais barbe d’intégriste n’a effleuré ses mimosas, jamais odeur de poudre n’a faussé les senteurs de sa félicité. Les nababs du bled y vivent en rentiers, la panse bien garnie, l’œil rivé sur le trip des cupidités."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
